# ESP-NOW power saving: the radio listens WINDOW ms of every INTERVAL ms
# (ESP-IDF "connectionless module power save": esp_now_set_wake_window +
# esp_wifi_connectionless_module_set_wake_interval, station interface only,
# needs CONFIG_ESP_WIFI_STA_DISCONNECTED_PM_ENABLE).  Between windows the RF is
# off and the CPU keeps running: this is modem sleep, not light sleep.
#
# ESP-IDF leaves window synchronisation to the application.  Here a sender
# retries every RETRY_DELAY ms (well below WINDOW) until the frame is
# acknowledged or RETRY_SPAN ms (>= INTERVAL) have passed, so one attempt is
# certain to fall inside the receiver's window.
#
# 50/100 ms are the defaults of ESP-IDF's examples/wifi/espnow.
CONFIG_TBFT_TRANSPORT_ESPNOW=y
CONFIG_EXAMPLE_ESPNOW_POWER_SAVE=y
CONFIG_EXAMPLE_ESPNOW_WAKE_WINDOW_MS=50
CONFIG_EXAMPLE_ESPNOW_WAKE_INTERVAL_MS=100
CONFIG_TBFT_ESPNOW_TX_RETRY_DELAY_MS=20
CONFIG_TBFT_ESPNOW_TX_RETRY_SPAN_MS=120
CONFIG_TBFT_ESPNOW_TX_RETRIES=3
